 "relevance_note": "One cohort patient (Table row 3) carries a biallelic ALDH5A1 variant: \"ALDH5A1:c.803G>A;p.Gly268Glu Biallelic | Pathogenic\".",
 "method_note": "Congenital ataxia cohort of 30 patients (WES); only the patient in row 3 of the paper's single clinical table carries an ALDH5A1 variant, so one in-scope individual; the other 29 get no rows. The table is unnumbered ('the Table'); its 'Patients' column holds bare numbers, and the text never says 'patient 3', so the label is 'Table 1 #3' (table treated as Table 1). Transcribed by hand; no script transcription. Zygosity 'homozygous' from the row ('Biallelic', one variant listed) plus the Discussion statement naming ALDH5A1 among genes with homozygous variants and the Figure 2 legend (a patient with a pathogenic homozygous ALDH5A1 mutation, global cerebellar hypoplasia), taken as this person. The paper never labels this patient as having SSADH deficiency; disease_label_as_stated is the row's congenital-ataxia classification. 'developmental delay' not mapped to motor deficits or intellectual disability (not specified). Ataxia/congenital ataxia rests on the cohort description (all 30 diagnosed with congenital ataxia) plus the row's congenital-ataxia classification; marked inferred from group statement. n_patients_reported=1 is read from the table (one ALDH5A1 row), not a stated number. Ethnicity 'Brazilian' from the cohort description. Age at onset not reported (inclusion criterion 'up to 3 years' not used). Contradictions in the paper (not about ALDH5A1): Discussion names MME patient as 'patient 20' (Table: 10), CACNA1A patients as 'Patients 28 and 30' (Table: 18 and 30), KIF1A as 'patient 18' (Table: 13); Table row numbering skips 14; Table row 30 classification cell repeats the variant.",
